-id pub-id-type="pmid">9585240</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b20-ijn-2-191"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Feng</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Ke</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Pharmacokinetics and long-term Gd tissue accumulation of (Gd-DTPA)-cystamine copolymers, a biodegradable macromolecular MRI contrast agent</article-title><source>Pharm Res</source><volume>22</volume><fpage>596</fpage><lpage>601</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15846467</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><fig id="f1-ijn-2-191" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Percentage of cell attachment of human prostate carcinoma DU145 cells and Kaposi&#x02019;s sarcoma SLK cells to the vitronectin-coated plates inhibited by MEM serum free media (control) or solutions of c(RGDfK) (RGD), c(RGDfK) containing PGA-cystamine-(Gd-DO3A) (RGDP), and PGA-cystamine-(Gd-DO3A) (P) at the concentrations of 5 &#x003bc;M (closed bar) and 50 &#x003bc;M (open bar). Values are shown as means &#x000b1; SD (n = 5). The &#x0201c;*&#x0201d; symbol indicates p &#x0003c; 0.05. The comparison is made to the control.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ijn-2-191f1"/></fig><fig id="f2-ijn-2-191" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>T<sub>1</sub>-weighted contrast enhanced coronal MR images of mice bearing human prostate carcinoma DU145 (left flank) and Kaposi&#x02019;s sarcoma SLK (right flank) xenografts before and at 8 minutes after injection of the c(RGDfK) containing PGA-cystamine-(Gd-DO3A) conjugate (A) and PGA-cystamine-(Gd-DO3A) (B).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ijn-2-191f2"/></fig><fig id="f3-ijn-2-191" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>T<sub>1</sub> maps of mice bearing human prostate carcinoma DU145 (left flank) and Kaposi&#x02019;s sarcoma SLK (right flank) xenografts before and after injection of the c(RGDfK) containing PGA-cystamine-(Gd-DO3A) conjugate (A) and PGA-cystamine-(Gd-DO3A) (B).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ijn-2-191f3"/></fig><fig id="f4-ijn-2-191" position="float"><label>Scheme 1</label><caption><p>Synthesis of RGD containing PGA-cystamine-(Gd-DO3A); i. DMAP, DMF, rt, 2 h; ii. DMAP, DMF, rt, 24 h. iii. Gd(OAc)<sub>3,</sub> Na<sub>2</sub>-EDTA, pH 5.5, rt, 24 h.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ijn-2-191f4"/></fig><table-wrap id="t1-ijn-2-191" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Physical chemical parameters of PGA-cystamine-(Gd-DO3A) and PGA-cystamine-(Gd-DO3A)-c(RGDfK) conjugates</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Property</bold></th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>PGA-cystamine-(Gd-DO3A)</bold></th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>PGA-cystamine-(Gd-DO3A)-c(RGDfK)</bold></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">M<sub>w</sub> (KDa)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">79.3</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">49</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">M<sub>w</sub>/M<sub>n</sub></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.81</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.89</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Gd content, (w/w)%<sup>b</sup></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">12.14</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">9.27</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Molar conjugation ratio</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">20.8</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">27</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">R<sub>1</sub> (mM<sup>&#x02212;1</sup>s<sup>&#x02212;1</sup>)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">7.8</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">9.7</td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>